# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER COMMIT THESE -- they hold private keys and this PC's PIN.
#
#   config.json   -> your account's PRIVATE KEY (relayToken). Anyone with it can
#                    register a PC as you.
#   device.json   -> this PC's device id and the 6-digit PIN that lets people
#                    connect to it.
#   PUBLIC-LINK.txt -> your live temporary tunnel address.
#
# A public repo (the Deploy to Cloudflare button needs one) would hand these to
# the whole internet. The repo carries config.json.example instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
config.json
device.json
PUBLIC-LINK.txt

# Cloudflare's local deploy state (caches, generated ids)
.wrangler/

# Dependencies -- reinstalled with `npm install`
node_modules/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Logs and stray captures
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Auto-generated folder/source dumps -- they duplicate the repo and go stale.
CURRENT_PROJECT_TREE.txt
CURRENT_PROJECT_SOURCE.txt

# Internal working notes for the AI agent, not part of the software.
AGENTS.md
